  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "What is the size of the largest $A\\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^d$ such that every three points from $A$ determine an isosceles triangle? That is, for any three points $x,y,z$ from $A$, at least two of the distances $\\lvert x-y\\rvert,\\lvert y-z\\rvert,\\lvert x-z\\rvert$ are equal.",
